# {{ appKey }} App

## Start here

- Read `nexia.json`, `composer.json`, `package.json`, `README.md`, and
  `docs/README.md` for this App's identity, commands, and domain design.
- Before changing platform calls, read the official App development guide:
  https://developers.nexia.to/docs/getting-started-agent-assisted-development
  With a CLI that supports documentation commands, use `nexia docs`,
  `nexia docs search "topic"`, and `nexia docs read <document-id>`.
  The guide links to public SDK contracts, examples, and validation procedures.
- Work in this App repository using public SDK contracts. Preserve its identity,
  existing work, migrations, and data. Missing platform capabilities belong in
  a support report, not a copied or patched platform implementation.

## App-owned guidance

Maintain this file with this App's responsibilities, domain constraints,
implementation conventions, and focused checks as they are established.
Keep shared Nexia guidance in the official documentation instead of copying it
here. This file belongs to the App developer after generation.

## Translation catalogs

- Keep `resources/lang/<locale>.json` flat with string values. Each value may
  contain at most 2,000 Unicode characters, including descriptions. Use
  `nexia check` at validation time to locate the file, key and length violations.
- The exported runtime catalog is limited to 1 MiB, 20 locales and 1,000 exported
  keys per locale. See the official localization guide for the shared contract:
  https://developers.nexia.to/docs/building-apps-localize-an-app
- Fix `CATALOG_VALIDATION_FAILED` declarations before retrying. Follow the
  operation's retry/review status; never delete `.nexia` or reset data to bypass it.

## Validation and delivery

- Use the checks documented in README.md. At validation time, start with
  `nexia check`, then verify the changed behavior and permissions in the sandbox.
  Report source checks, observed runtime behavior, and unverified items separately.
- Draft changes defer automated checks until testing, verification, finalization,
  commit, push, or PR is requested. Run the smallest relevant check then.
- Use a purpose-named branch. Do not commit, push, submit, merge, publish,
  reset data, or send messages without authorization. Never expose credentials.
